winevulkan: Let a VR runtime enable VK_EXT_metal_objects on macOS.

wineopenxr hands DXVK the device extensions the OpenXR runtime asks for through
VK_WINE_openxr_device_extensions, and win32u enables them on the host device by name from the
extension table make_vulkan generates. VK_EXT_metal_objects was listed as unsupported (an
extension for another platform), so it had no entry and was dropped. OXRSys exports its Vulkan
swapchain images to Metal with it and refuses to create color swapchains without it.

make_vulkan now lists it with the other unexposed macOS extensions (VK_EXT_metal_surface): win32u
can enable it on the host device, and Windows applications still do not see it. Only
include/wine/vulkan.h changes when regenerated against Vulkan 1.4.335; the thunks are identical.

